<h2>Do Claude Code plugins install in Grok Build?</h2>
<p class="answer">Yes: Grok Build supports Claude Code marketplaces alongside xAI's own marketplace, so most Claude Code plugins install there with two documented exceptions: Claude Code LSP plugins and ambiguous names that exist in multiple marketplaces.</p>
[[SMX:GROK_VS_CLAUDE_PLUGINS_HTML]]
<p>When the same plugin name appears in both xAI's marketplace and Claude Code's marketplace (examples documented in our <a href="/guides/what-installs-in-grok-build/">What installs in Grok Build</a> guide include <code>auth0</code>, <code>grafana-mcp</code>, <code>postman</code> and <code>pr-review-toolkit</code>), Grok Build asks you to disambiguate with <code>name@marketplace</code>. Meanwhile, Claude Code LSP plugins (such as language-server plugins) only target Claude Code.</p>

